WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.683
A useful deployment starts with clear ownership and

00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:07.016
a few deliberate checks before the first users

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:07.433
arrive.

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:12.536
Confirm the intended public address, persistent storage, and

00:00:12.536 --> 00:00:17.240
operational responsibilities. Configure the required settings through your

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.943
deployment’s documented process, keeping secret values out of

00:00:21.943 --> 00:00:22.531
recordings.

00:00:22.931 --> 00:00:26.034
Complete the first-run owner setup. Then verify that

00:00:26.034 --> 00:00:29.137
setup is closed and that the owner can

00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:31.464
sign in through the intended route.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:35.416
Define the units and assign roles deliberately. Check

00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:38.968
a new member before and after attachment so

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:42.076
the unit’s information appears only where intended.

00:00:42.476 --> 00:00:46.612
Verify the workflows the deployment relies on: sign-in,

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:50.747
membership, saving a record, and reporting. Test backup

00:00:50.747 --> 00:00:54.883
recovery in staging. A successful homepage is not

00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:56.951
a complete deployment check.

00:00:57.351 --> 00:01:01.407
Record who owns the deployment and how users

00:01:01.407 --> 00:01:05.463
get help. Keep a dated configuration and verification

00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:09.519
record. VANTAGE is independent software; deploying it does

00:01:09.519 --> 00:01:11.547
not establish official approval.
